Two AI-facing documents, for two different jobs:

- Editing this repository → `CLAUDE.md` (build invariants; each exists because it was
  violated silently in the past, and none are caught by `cargo test`).
- Using the published plugin → `AGENTS.md` (id-naming specification).

Before reporting any change complete, run:

```bash
./scripts/check-invariants.sh && cargo test && cargo build --target wasm32-wasip1 --release
```

Non-zero from `check-invariants.sh` means re-run with `--fix`, then hand-fix the rest.

Highest-value traps:

- `cargo test` never crosses the plugin FFI boundary — a dependency-pin mismatch passes
  the suite and fails only at the WASM link step. Always run the WASM build.
- A new fixture directory is silently not run until `touch tests/fixture.rs`, because
  `#[testing::fixture]` expands its glob at compile time.
- Never swallow a `Result` in `src/lib.rs` — the WASI sandbox turns a swallowed error
  into a silent no-op, and config deserialization is all-or-nothing.
- Every generated identifier must reuse the source binding's `Ident` (`sym` *and*
  `SyntaxContext`), or a minifier will not rename it and the build breaks only under
  minification.
- Do not publish or commit without an explicit request.
